### Why the skip is not a hole

1. **Front door always runs on emit-c / llvm / check.** SECRET IDENT at
   `println`/`eprintln` `process_exit`s in `check_secret_println_sinks`
   **before** `c_emit_println` or `c_secret_emit_guard` is reached.
   Live eprintln refuse is **not** proof stmt println was unified
   (`s29_integration.oot`).
2. **Same IDENT set.** Check walk and stmt walk both see source IDENT
   tokens (not STRING). Guard C-text scan sees the same names after
   `c_emit_expr_c` (`tok` → `tok` / `oo_str_concat(..., tok)`). Path-A
   has no STRING_TEMPLATE splice (5.8 residual) and no macro expand (2.8).
3. **Alias resolve gap is not a data FN.**
   - `c_secret_refuse_println_ident` checks `__sec__name` only.
   - Guard / check use `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` (`__alias__` then
     `__sec__`).
   - `__alias__` is recorded **only** for sink names (`c_secret_is_sink_name`
     / `c_secret_try_record_alias_rhs`). Data aliases (`let x = tok`) are
     `__sec__x=1` via `c_secret_prop_from_rhs` — both belts refuse `x`.
   - Callee alias `let f = println; f(tok)` never enters `c_emit_println`
     (`id == "f"`). It is free-call → full guard, **and** the check walk
     resolves `sid`.
4. **s71 Z2 already proved skip ≠ fail-open.** This turn re-proves the
   refuse contract; does not reopen 7.1 walker memory.

### Why DE2.9 is not a land (honesty)

SPRINT “What got fixed” DE2.9 (`c_emit_secret.oo:175-186` →
`c_secret_emit_guard(env, id, ...)`) is **false on disk**. Those lines
are the IDENT loop + `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`. The guard wants
lowered C `a0/a1/a2/args`. A check-path call is the wrong signature
(ideas I9 — disqualified). Close 2.9 as **dual refuse**, not as that
sentence.

### 6.1 / s71 sentences this OWN answers

- **6.1** (`check_drive.oo`): SECRET walk moved **before** typecheck so
  unlowered sinks still dual-path. Host ELF is still type-then-secret
  (s61 smoke check type-first). Product `println` is a **known** name →
  check still prints `ERR\tsecret` on IDENT refuse (not type-first).
- **s71_security R1 / Z2:** stmt `println` never calls `c_guard_scan_idents`.
  Token + check dual still BLOCK. Unify later = this ticket. Equivalent
  refuse ⇒ no surgical route.

